    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0514" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5961</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Luther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-01">October 1, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have noted with special interest
                    the official announcement, communicated by Your Excellency’s note of September
                    16, 1935, of the new arrangement for purchase of Dawes and Young Loan coupons,
                    which, as you have intimated, is designed to remove some of the financial
                    disadvantages and technical difficulties with which American holders seeking to
                    receive interest payment on the bonds have until now been confronted and as a
                    contribution toward the settlement of problems pending between the two
                    Governments.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
